why: RFC 5234 requires CRLF line endings
- crlf = (byte 0x0D *> byte 0x0A) <?> "CRLF"
+ crlf = (optional (byte 0x0D) *> byte 0x0A) <?> "CRLF"

why: comments are WSP and VCHAR only
- comment = byte 0x3B *> void (takeWhile0 (\w -> isWSP w || isVChar w)) *> crlf
+ comment = byte 0x3B *> void (takeWhile0 (\w -> w /= 0x0D)) *> crlf

why: the elements of a concatenation are separated by whitespace
